WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue {
    color: white;
    background-color: #383943A3;
}

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.585
Welcome to Primark and Penneys.

00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:07.205
Before you start on the shop floor, we'll take you
through the health, safety and environment essentials

00:00:07.205 --> 00:00:08.333
for our stores.

00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:11.919
There are six short videos, followed by a short exam.

00:00:11.919 --> 00:00:15.553
Pass it, and you'll receive a certificate to bring
with you on your first day.

00:00:17.353 --> 00:00:22.089
From your very first shift, you'll be working around
customers, stock and equipment.

00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:24.666
Most accidents in stores are avoidable.

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:27.673
They are prevented by people who notice something
and act on it.

00:00:27.673 --> 00:00:29.380
That's what this course is about.

00:00:31.181 --> 00:00:33.039
Safety is shared.

00:00:33.039 --> 00:00:38.227
Primark's job is to give you a safe place to work,
and to find and control hazards.

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:44.045
Your job is to work safely, follow the procedures
you're shown, use equipment and safety gear properly,

00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:47.168
and make sure nothing you do puts anyone else at risk.

00:00:47.168 --> 00:00:48.317
No shortcuts.

00:00:50.117 --> 00:00:53.112
If something happens, tell your supervisor straight
away.

00:00:53.112 --> 00:01:00.670
That includes any accident or injury, however minor,
to anyone: you, a colleague, a customer or a contractor.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:06.348
It also covers damaged equipment, any hazard you spot,
and any health problem you think is linked to your

00:01:06.348 --> 00:01:09.134
work, such as back pain from lifting.

00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:15.519
Every accident is recorded on the same day, in the
Accident Book and on the A-R-C-C system.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.606
Every store has trained first aiders and first aid
boxes.

00:01:20.744 --> 00:01:25.829
You'll find who they are, and where the boxes are
kept, on the store notice board, so check it on your

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:26.723
first shift.

00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:30.787
Your store also has a Safety Committee that meets
regularly to represent you.

00:01:30.787 --> 00:01:34.781
You can raise any safety concern with them, as well
as with your manager.

00:01:36.581 --> 00:01:43.675
Remember: notice hazards, report accidents or concerns
straight away, and never take shortcuts.

00:01:43.675 --> 00:01:46.983
Small actions on the shop floor help keep everyone
safe.